'''Infernal Tyrant Nyandam''' (大魔王ニャンダム, ''Daimaō Nyandamu'', '''Great Demon King Nyandam''') is an [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] variant of [[Dark Emperor Nyandam]] that appears in the [[:Category:Advent Stages#Great Advent Stages|Great Advent Stage]] [[Reign of the Tyrant]]. He was added in [[Version 12.3 Update|Version 12.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Infernal Tyrant Nyandam
|image = E 642.png
|appearance = [[Reign of the Tyrant]]
|money drop = 6,666¢ - 26,330¢
}}

==Enemy==
With some of the highest stats in the game, this enemy is truly devastating. His first hit essentially destroys everything he hits at normal range, and if that wasn't enough, he will hit the backlines with a 30% Toxic attack through his second and third hits. Combined with his immunities to knockback, weaken and [[Surge Attack|surge]] effects, extreme health and three knockbacks, he can prove a nightmare even to the best prepared, especially when his support enters play.

He is not fully unbeatable, however. His second and third hits have two blind spots between 400-500 and 800-1000 respectively, so units within these areas are safe until he pushes. 30% Toxic is a big number, but may not impede you from sending more units to stall him.

==Strategy==
This enemy can be stalled just fine with [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Macho]] or [[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cats]]. The actual issue is keeping an army alive to deal with his supporters. One of the best ways to do so involves using the [[Ototo Corps|Thunderbolt Cannon]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Li'l Axe Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Dark Cat]], [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N201 (Special Cat)|Exorcist Cat]]. His animation is a bit short for a Nyandam variant and he is immune to knockback, so you will have to rely on [[Battle Items|Sniper the Cat]] or the default [[Cat Cannon]] to buy a bit of extra time. The approach will differ depending on other supporting enemies in the stage for an opportunity to freeze Nyandam and quickly remove him.

Alternatively, you may wish to exploit Infernal Tyrant Nyandam's blind spots and attack from range. Certain units, such as [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]], can be slowly accumulated in the safe spots just in front of big hitters or stallers, forming a layered, last line of defence for when Infernal Tyrant Nyandam advances while helping out against the support. Notably good units (without going into stage specifics) include: [[Chronos]], [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Shisilan Pasalan]],  [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Summoner Satoru]], [[Yuletide Nurse (Uber Rare Cat)|Xmas Spirit Nurse]], [[Goddess of Light Sirius (Uber Rare Cat)|Goddess of Light Sirius]], [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]], [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] (those last two both standing in the further blind spot), and most attackers with range between 401 and 499, as long as they have enough speed to ignore some Toxic attacks or are immune anyways. Keep in mind that such units should not be used in hopes of defeating Infernal Tyrant Nyandam fast, but rather to aid the meatshields in stopping his advance and to clear his support as fast or as safely as possible. Also note, with Cosmo's high speed, he'll run into a bad spot if Nyandam is knocked back, so don't use the Sniper The Cat item if you're using Cosmo.

Lastly, non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] rushdown attackers can be used to chip away at Infernal Tyrant Nyandam's health during the openings, with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] being a good example for doing fair amounts of additional damage.

