==Trivia==
*Based on how his Japanese name is Great Demon King Nyandam, this enemy appears to have been foreshadowed several times prior to his release.
**[[Dark Emperor Nyandam]]'s Japanese description states he dyed his body [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] in order to feel drunk, implying the existence of an earlier, non-Red form of Nyandam.
**[[Prince of Darkness]]'s and [[Satan's Bedroom]]'s Japanese names can be translated as "Demon King's Mansion" and "Demon King's Bedroom" respectively. The latter also shares its [[Backgrounds|background]] with [[Infernal Tyrant 1 (Deadly)|Infernal Tyrant 1]]. Furthermore, Dark Emperor Nyandam also appears in [[Dictator's Garden]], the fifth stage in Prince of Darkness.
**[[Cat Clan Heroes (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Clan Heroes]]' Japanese description states that their group was formed to defeat the Demon King. However, this so-called Demon King may instead refer to [[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss]], another unit in the same set.
**[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]]'s description claims he sealed away the Demon King. The Japanese version clarifies that he ordered his cockatoo to say it, and as such the validity of this statement is questionable. It however may be also refer to [[Lord of Ruin Jagando|Jagando]], who was once sealed by great heroes.
**[[Possessed by Evil (Merciless)|Possessed by Evil]]'s Japanese name is Possessed by the Demon King, implying that [[Evil Emperor Cat]] is actually possessed by Nyandam.
**[[Sathankhamun VIII]] wears a blue Nyandam mask and his Japanese description associates him with the second coming of a Great Demon King.
*If the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]] are the Seven Deadly Sins, then Infernal Tyrant Nyandam likely represents Satan himself. 魔王 (''Maō'', lit. "Demon King") can even be translated as "Satan" or "The Devil".
*Infernal Tyrant Nyandam's return is implied to be only temporary. His English description mentions him going on a blind date, whereas in Japanese, he was to appear in a marriage photo shoot.
*[[Xenobeast Bunaglios]] can be seen as a foil to Infernal Tyrant Nyandam. Both are blue, four-horned, knockback-immune Great Advent Boss variants of [[Empire of Cats]] [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon/Iriomote]] bosses with 400 range and hand-based attacks, but Nyandam is darker, attacks with hands made of darkness, and voluntarily took his current form for a marriage photo shoot, while Bunaglios is lighter, attacks with a hand that radiates light, and wound up in the wild against his will.
*He has the highest attack power and DPS of all [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] enemies and [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], has the highest maximum effective range of all Aku, and is tied with [[Aku Cyclone]] for the highest money drop of all Aku.
*He has the second highest heath of all [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]  enemies, only beaten by [[Malevolent Eraser Cat]].
*Many of his stats contain the number 666, a number known as 'the number of the beast.'

